language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ car_selection: an Essence' model from DCP Rosetta.
$
$ Assign participants to cars so as to maximise the total number of assignments. Each participant may be interested in a subset of the available cars. Each participant is assigned to at most one car, and each car is assigned to at most one participant.
$
$ Save this file as model.eprime. Download `car_selection.json` and `dcp_convert_essence.py` from the
$ problem's page:
$   https://dcp-bench.github.io/DCP-Rosetta/problems/car_selection.html
$ Convert the instances once, then run the first one with Savile Row 1.11 (it needs Java); the
$ solution is written to `car_selection_1.param.solution`:
$   python dcp_convert_essence.py car_selection.json
$   savilerow model.eprime car_selection_1.param -run-solver

$ number of participants and number of cars, derived from the data: the row count and the row length of possible_assignments (not fields of the reader's JSON)
given possible_assignments_dim1 : int(1..)
given possible_assignments_dim2 : int(1..)
$ possible_assignments[i,j]: 1 if participant i is interested in car j, 0 otherwise, indices 1-based
given possible_assignments : matrix indexed by [int(1..possible_assignments_dim1), int(1..possible_assignments_dim2)] of int(0..1)

$ assignments[i,j]: participant i is assigned to car j
find assignments : matrix indexed by [int(1..possible_assignments_dim1), int(1..possible_assignments_dim2)] of bool
$ total: the number of assignments made, which is maximised
find total : int(0..possible_assignments_dim1 * possible_assignments_dim2)

maximising total
such that
$ the total is the number of participant-car pairs that are assigned
total = (sum i : int(1..possible_assignments_dim1) . sum j : int(1..possible_assignments_dim2) . toInt(assignments[i,j])),
$ a participant is assigned only to a car that participant is interested in
forAll i : int(1..possible_assignments_dim1) . forAll j : int(1..possible_assignments_dim2) . assignments[i,j] -> possible_assignments[i,j] = 1,
$ each participant is assigned to at most one car
forAll i : int(1..possible_assignments_dim1) . (sum j : int(1..possible_assignments_dim2) . toInt(assignments[i,j])) <= 1,
$ each car is assigned to at most one participant
forAll j : int(1..possible_assignments_dim2) . (sum i : int(1..possible_assignments_dim1) . toInt(assignments[i,j])) <= 1
